.TH MU2EDAQ_DISCOVERY 3 "2026-09-30" "mu2edaq-discovery 1.1.0" "Mu2e DAQ Manual"
.SH NAME
mu2edaq_discovery \- Python library for Mu2e DAQ service discovery
.SH SYNOPSIS
.EX
from mu2edaq_discovery import Responder, discover, protocol

r = Responder(name, app, port, scheme=None, version=None, meta=None,
              host=None, group=protocol.GROUP, listen_port=protocol.PORT,
              announce_interval=0, bind_interface=None)
r.start()
r.stop(timeout=2.0)

services = discover(filter=None, timeout=2.0, retries=2,
                    group=protocol.GROUP, port=protocol.PORT,
                    interface=None, broadcast=True)
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mu2edaq_discovery
implements the
.B mu2edaq\-discovery/1
wire protocol described in
.BR mu2edaq\-discovery (7).
It is stdlib\-only and targets Python 3.9, so it imports under the AlmaLinux 9
system interpreter with no virtualenv and no third\-party packages.
.PP
The module has two halves.
A service embeds a
.B Responder
so it can be found; an operator tool calls
.B discover()
to find services.
.SS Responder
.B Responder
is a subclass of
.BR threading.Thread ,
constructed as a daemon thread named
.BR mu2edaq\-discovery\-responder .
It binds UDP
.I listen_port
on
.BR 0.0.0.0 ,
joins the multicast group on
.IR bind_interface ,
and answers every DISCOVER whose filter it matches with a unicast ANNOUNCE
sent back to the datagram's source address and port, after a uniform random
delay of 0 to 250 ms
.RB ( Responder.JITTER_MAX )
that spreads a fleet's replies.
.TP
.I name
Human\-readable label, shown in the
.B NAME
column.
.TP
.I app
Short class identifier.
Instances sharing an
.I app
are grouped in the GUI, and
.B \-\-filter\ app=
selects them.
.TP
.I port
The service's own listening port, as an integer.
This is the port the announcement advertises, not the discovery port.
.TP
.I scheme
URL scheme hint
.RB ( http ,
.BR vnc ,
.BR tcp ,
.BR udp ).
Defaults to
.IR app .
.TP
.I version
Free\-form version string.
Defaults to
.BR "0" .
.TP
.I meta
A mapping of string keys to string values for application\-specific detail.
The GUI renders each as a
.BI meta. key
column.
Both keys and values must be strings or the receiving side rejects the
message.
.TP
.I host
Advertised hostname.
Defaults to
.BR socket.getfqdn() ,
re\-resolved on every announcement.
.TP
.I announce_interval
Seconds between unsolicited ANNOUNCE multicasts.
Zero, the default, means the responder answers queries only.
.TP
.I bind_interface
Local IPv4 address used for the multicast group membership and as
.BR IP_MULTICAST_IF .
Defaults to
.BR 0.0.0.0 .
.PP
.B start()
returns immediately; the socket is opened on the responder thread, so a bind
or membership failure does not reach the caller and leaves a dead thread
behind.
Poll
.B is_alive()
if that matters.
.B stop()
sets the stop event, sends a zero\-length datagram to
.BI 127.0.0.1: listen_port
to break the 0.5 s
.BR recvfrom (2)
timeout, and joins with
.IR timeout .
Calling
.B stop()
on a responder that was never started raises
.BR RuntimeError .
.SS discover
.B discover()
sends one DISCOVER to the multicast group and, unless
.I broadcast
is false or empty, the same datagram to each named broadcast address.
It transmits
.I retries
times spread across the
.I timeout
window, collects ANNOUNCE datagrams until
.I timeout
seconds have elapsed in total, discards replies carrying a
.B qid
that is not this query's, deduplicates by the responder's stable
.BR id ,
and returns a list of message dicts sorted by
.RI ( host ", " port ).
.PP
.I broadcast
accepts
.BR True ,
.BR False ,
a list of addresses, or a string:
.BR on / yes / true / default
for the limited broadcast,
.BR off / no / false / none
for none, or addresses separated by commas or whitespace.
.B parse_broadcast_setting()
is the single normaliser the CLI, the GUI, the environment and the API all
share.
.SS protocol
The
.B protocol
submodule holds the constants
.RB ( PROTO ,
.BR GROUP ,
.BR PORT ,
.BR BROADCAST ,
.BR MAX_DATAGRAM ,
.BR FILTER_KEYS )
and the message builders and validators
.RB ( build_query ,
.BR build_announce ,
.BR encode ,
.BR decode ,
.BR matches_filter ).
.B encode()
and
.B decode()
both raise
.BR protocol.ProtocolError ,
a subclass of
.BR ValueError ,
on an oversize or malformed message.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I src/mu2edaq_discovery/protocol.py
Constants, builders and validators.
.TP
.I src/mu2edaq_discovery/responder.py
.BR Responder .
.TP
.I src/mu2edaq_discovery/client.py
.B discover()
and
.BR parse_broadcast_setting() .
.SH ENVIRONMENT
The library itself reads no environment variables; the
.BR mu2edaq\-discover (1)
and
.BR mu2edaq\-discover\-gui (1)
front ends read the
.B MU2EDAQ_DISCOVERY_*
set.
.SH EXAMPLES
Advertise a Flask dashboard after its socket is bound:
.EX
    from mu2edaq_discovery import Responder

    responder = Responder(name="Mu2e DAQ Dashboard", app="dashboard",
                          port=5001, scheme="http",
                          meta={"zmq_port": "5555"})
    responder.start()
    try:
        app.run(host="0.0.0.0", port=5001)
    finally:
        responder.stop()
.EE
Find every VNC session on the subnet:
.EX
    from mu2edaq_discovery import discover

    for s in discover(filter={"app": "vnc"}, timeout=2.0):
        print(s["host"], s["port"], s["meta"].get("display"))
.EE
Multicast only, for diagnosing IGMP snooping:
.EX
    discover(broadcast=False)
.EE
.SH NOTES
The
.I meta
map counts against the 1400\-byte datagram limit, and the limit is checked on
the serialized message.
A responder whose ANNOUNCE crosses it raises inside the responder thread on
the first query and stops answering for the life of the process.
.PP
IPv4 only.
The sockets are
.BR AF_INET ,
the group membership is
.BR ip_mreq ,
and there is no IPv6 path.
